     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nWas it a typo or a unit mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day) is the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, at a frequency you choose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. I'd still recommend against it."
      }
     ],
